Faster reduced poly2d product for 128-bit coefficients

Add mul_reduce, the product of two poly2d reduced in the inner variable, and use it for QuickSilver
products. For 128-bit coefficients, it computes the Karatsuba half sums once per input coefficient,
and accumulates the uncombined CLMUL results of each output coefficient before interpolating,
recombining, and reducing it once.

TODO Propose this change to faest-arch-opt authors.

